      <h3 class="text-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4">
        The load is where the serving size enters
      </h3>
      <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The glycemic load multiplies the index by the grams of available carbohydrate in the
        serving and divides by 100. Available carbohydrate means total carbohydrate minus fibre,
        which is the definition used when the tables were compiled. The calculator does exactly
        that arithmetic on its own rows, so the load it shows can always be reproduced from the
        index, carbohydrate and fibre beside it.
      </p>

